    {
      "id": "decision:staged-reevaluation-with-kill-gates",
      "type": "Decision",
      "label": "Re-evaluate the graph in staged steps with numeric kill criteria (step 0: fast reads + companion rerun)",
      "description": "What: step 0 (~1 day) fix kg's read latency and rerun the 16 scrapy questions with a companion strategy, kill if score drops > 0.03 or context > +15% or time > +30% vs code; step 1 (3-5 days) TYPE_CHECKING, inherits, settings/dotted-path facts on 12 externally checked hard questions; step 2 (~1 week) MCP server and a docs/settings drift check.\nWhy: the council found part of the scrapy loss was kg's implementation, and the old benchmark tested graph instead of grep, which no published system claims.\nWhere: issue #67\nLearned: step 0 failed on time, so steps 1 and 2 were never run.",
      "attrs": {
