    {
      "id": "decision:validation-cache-content-addressed",
      "type": "Decision",
      "label": "load_graph skips schema validation for content kg already validated, via a content-addressed marker in the user cache",
      "description": "What: marker in $XDG_CACHE_HOME/kg/validated/ keyed by SHA-256 of the contents, kg's version and the schema; written on save or after a full validation on load; any edit triggers full validation; unwritable cache means full validation every time; store format unchanged.\nWhy: re-validating scrapy's 11.5 MB store took 5-10 s per command, about half of the graph strategies' wall time.\nWhere: src/kg/store.py, src/kg/schema/validation.py (validate_bytes), docs/store.md, tests/conftest.py (autouse fixture so tests never write the real cache)\nLearned: kg query on scrapy 4.94 s -> 0.84 s; first read of an unseen document still validates (7-11 s on scrapy); benchmark prepare warms the cache because saving marks the store as validated.",
      "attrs": {
        "status": "active",
        "session": "session:2026-10-20-84137a84",
