    {
      "id": "decision:companion-and-lean-strategies",
      "type": "Decision",
      "label": "Benchmark adds companion (code tools + kg --brief) and the lean control (code tools + the same 'fewer calls' prompt line)",
      "description": "What: companion gives list_files, read_file, search plus kg with --brief and the report counts runs that call kg; lean is code with companion's prompt line, to separate prompt effect from graph effect.\nWhy: earlier graph strategies forbade free reading, testing 'graph instead of grep'; companion runs read less even without calling kg, so a control was needed.\nWhere: bench/tools.py, bench/run.py, bench/report.py, bench/README.md\nLearned: when measuring any tool, compare against both code and lean and fix the win criterion before running.",
