    {
      "id": "experiment:step0-companion-scrapy",
      "type": "Experiment",
      "label": "Step 0 on scrapy: companion 0.96 vs code 0.98, -40% context, +45% time; gate fails on time",
      "description": "What: 80 Opus subagent runs (companion x2, cards x2, code x1) on the 16 scrapy questions with the fast kg, plus the earlier code run: code 0.98 / 8 731 chars / 31.8 s, companion 0.96 / 5 199 / 46.0 s, cards 0.95 / 19 166 / 50.4 s.\nWhy: separate 'the concept failed' from 'the implementation failed'.\nWhere: bench/results/20261020T090411Z-subagent-scrapy-step0.jsonl, ...090412Z..., docs/benchmark.md 'Update: a large repo, scrapy'\nLearned: companion called kg in 15/32 runs (impact, path, test questions), 63.6 s vs 30.5 s without kg; scr-impact-job-runtime fails with every strategy (needs TYPE_CHECKING-aware imports); one run cut by the session limit was resumed and its time (146 s) estimated without the outage; two runs hit the 25-call cap and count as failures.",
      "attrs": {
