    {
      "id": "experiment:lean-control-scrapy",
      "type": "Experiment",
      "label": "lean control: prompt line explains the saving where kg is unused; where used, kg halves context at equal score but costs ~1/3 more time",
      "description": "What: 16 lean runs on scrapy. 8 questions where companion never called kg: lean 1.00 / 2 851 chars / 25.7 s vs companion 0.99 / 2 851 / 30.3 s. 7 where it did: lean 0.99 / 9 816 / 35.1 s vs companion 0.98 / 4 299 (-56%) / 47.4 s (+35%). job-runtime: lean 1.00 / 104 s, companion 0.50 / 163 s.\nWhy: test the hypothesis that companion's context saving came from the prompt line, not the graph.\nWhere: bench/results/20261020T130120Z-subagent-scrapy-lean.jsonl, docs/benchmark.md, #67 comment\nLearned: corrected the earlier claim that the saving is not kg's: it is the prompt where kg is unused, kg where it is used; the graph never improves accuracy and hurts on the type-only-imports question; gate still fails.",
      "attrs": {
        "status": "done",
